      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To determine the number of women who attended the party, we need to analyze the given information and use it to set up an equation.\n\n1. **Identify the total number of dances per man:**\n   Each man danced with exactly 3 women.\n\n2. **Identify the total number of dances per woman:**\n   Each woman danced with exactly 2 men.\n\n3. **Calculate the total number of dances:**\n   Since there are 12 men and each man danced with 3 women, the total number of dances is:\n   \\[\n   12 \\text{ men} \\times 3 \\text{ women/man} = 36 \\text{ dances}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Determine the total number of dances from the women's perspective:**\n   Since each woman danced with 2 men, the total number of dances can also be calculated as:\n   \\[\n   12 \\text{ women} \\times 2 \\text{ men/woman} = 24 \\text{ dances}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Set up the equation to find the number of women:**\n   The total number of dances is the same whether we count them from the men's or the women's perspective. Therefore, we can set up the equation:\n   \\[\n   12 \\text{ men} \\times 3 \\text{ women/man} = 24 \\text{ women}\n   \\]\n\n6. **Solve for the number of women:**\n   Simplify the equation:\n   \\[\n   36 \\text{ dances} = 24 \\text{ women}\n   \\]\n   Solving for the number of women:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of women} = \\frac{36}{24} = 1.5\n   \\]\n\nThus, the number of women who attended the party is \\(\\boxed{1.5}\\).",
